```c
for (size_t i = 0; i < addr_sets->n_values; i++) {
    cs->values[cs->n_values++] = addr_sets->values[i];
}
```

This does a struct copy of the entire `union expr_constant`. If the addr_set values were created with uninitialized fields...

Let me look at `expr_const_sets_add` - that's in the test file.

